---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import WebsitePilotGuide from '../../components/WebsitePilotGuide.astro';
import WebsiteVisitorWorksheet from '../../components/WebsiteVisitorWorksheet.astro';
import {websitePilotMaterials} from '../../data/website-pilots.mjs';
import {url} from '../../lib/site';
const communities = [
 {name:'NTEN community', body:'A nonprofit-technology community that welcomes staff, volunteers, funders, consultants and vendors. Its public entry page says community access needs a free account; paid membership is separate.', limit:'Ask the Community team about the right group and invitation rules before offering services or recruiting participants.', links:[['Community entry','https://www.nten.org/connect'],['Participation questions','https://www.nten.org/contact'],['Code of conduct','https://www.nten.org/code-of-conduct']]},
 {name:'Opportunity Hack', body:'A year-round social-good technology community. Its signup page invites developers, designers and data practitioners to a free Slack community for collaboration around nonprofit projects.', limit:'The specific rules for outside projects and pilot invitations need organizer confirmation. Start with the general inquiry form.', links:[['Community entry','https://www.ohack.dev/signup'],['Ask an organizer','https://www.ohack.dev/contact']]},
 {name:'TechSoup community and Connect', body:'TechSoup’s 2021 announcement describes Connect as the successor to NetSquared. Qualification for technology offers is a separate process.', limit:'Current event and forum access was limited in this review. Confirm current availability, eligibility and participation rules through the official support route.', links:[['2021 program announcement','https://blog.techsoup.org/en-us/posts/techsoup-connect-your-new-community-events-program'],['Offer qualification','https://support.techsoup.org/hc/en-us/articles/360053429954-Qualification-Status-Locating-and-Understanding-the-Status-in-Your-TechSoup-Account'],['Current support route','https://support.techsoup.org/hc/en-us/requests/new']]}
];
---
<Base title="Website improvements and Charity OS pilots" description="Start with one useful website change, review a private concept and choose whether a separate, bounded Charity OS pilot fits your team.">
<header class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><Crumbs items={[{label:'For charities',href:'/for-charities/'},{label:'Website improvements and pilots'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">An invitation to build and learn · practice draft 0.1</p><h1>Make one useful change.<br />Learn with the team.</h1><p class="lede">A clearer volunteer page, a simpler handover or a more visible next step. Begin with a job your team wants to improve, then inspect a proposed change before choosing what to adopt.</p><div class="pilot-actions"><a class="btn" href="#case-guide">Prepare a case file</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#visitor-task-worksheet">Compare a visitor task</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:hello@charitology.org?subject=Charitology%20website%20preview&body=Official%20website%3A%0AOne%20visitor%20task%3A%0AMy%20role%3A%0A">Discuss a website preview</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#pilot">Explore a one-workflow OS pilot</a></div></div></header>
<div class="wrap pilot-body">
<section class="prose"><h2>Improve the system around the work.</h2><p>Follow the signals, channels, work, outcomes and feedback around one task. A volunteer page can help someone find a relevant role; a review process can clarify who decides what happens next. The proposed improvement still needs testing with the people using it.</p><p>Relief, repair, prevention, structure and source describe where work acts. Every level may be needed. This program studies mechanisms and practical friction; it does not rate charities or judge the good they do.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="path-title"><p class="eyebrow">An inspectable starting point</p><h2 id="path-title">From a public page to an agreed next step.</h2><ol class="pilot-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Choose one visitor task.</h3><p>Read the charity’s current official pages and agree what matters: finding a role, understanding a program or reaching the correct contact. Record observed behavior separately from assumptions about its effects.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Prepare a private concept.</h3><p>Use original draft copy and appropriately licensed material. Label the version, proposed changes and limitations. Keep actual donations, applications and sensitive information on the charity’s existing authorized routes.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Let the charity decide.</h3><p>The charity chooses whether to use any change. Confirm who can approve the exact version, its hosting, rights, checks, backup and rollback before publication. A preview does not replace the official website.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Review what actually happened.</h3><p>Record useful feedback and problems after any agreed use. A cleaner layout, completed task or favorable comment is not proof of extra donations or mission impact. Change the proposal when the evidence calls for it.</p></div></li></ol></section>
<WebsitePilotGuide />
<WebsiteVisitorWorksheet />
<section class="pilot-choice"><p class="eyebrow">Two separate choices</p><h2>Website help can stand on its own.</h2><p>An OS pilot is optional. Declining it should not change an agreed website contribution. A conversation also does not establish a service engagement, delivery deadline, account, migration or institutional partnership; we agree the actual scope and capacity with each team.</p></section>
<section id="pilot"><p class="eyebrow">One workflow · fictional records first</p><h2>Try a small Charity OS pilot.</h2><p class="prose">Choose a task such as a volunteer handover, a grant review or finding the source behind a decision. The following two-week sequence is an editable proposal, not a validated timetable or an already completed study.</p><div class="pilot-grid"><article><h3>Agree the question.</h3><p>Choose a responsible role, one fictional example and what the current process does well. Keep baseline values unknown until someone observes them. Agree a stop decision and a way to disagree.</p></article><article><h3>Try the actual work.</h3><p>Exercise the relevant permissions, review, approval and export/recovery steps. Count setup and help time as well as task time. Keep difficulties and missing capabilities visible.</p></article><article><h3>Review and revise.</h3><p>Separate bugs, unclear wording, training questions and missing features. Inspect the exact changed version. A descriptive comparison from one team does not establish causal or general benefit.</p></article><article><h3>Choose what comes next.</h3><p>Continue, revise, pause, stop or keep the current tool. Agree cleanup and access. Publishing a name, logo, quotation or case study requires its own permission.</p></article></div><p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@charitology.org?subject=Charitology%20one-workflow%20pilot&body=One%20workflow%3A%0AWhat%20already%20works%3A%0AMy%20role%3A%0A">Discuss a pilot</a></p><p class="prose">Existing <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/projects">Projects and tasks</a> and <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/resources">Resources</a> can support an agreed example after sign-in and organization choice. These links create no record or access grant. The <a href={url('/for-charities/os-plan/')}>implementation plan</a> explains current scope and remaining specialist/integration work.</p></section>
<section id="shift-handoff-pilot" class="pilot-choice" aria-labelledby="shift-handoff-pilot-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">An open invitation · volunteer coordinators</p>
  <h2 id="shift-handoff-pilot-title">Practice one volunteer shift handoff.</h2>
  <p>Try a made-up shift with a coordinator and two adults who choose to take part. Both volunteers can read and agree to their own part of the change. The confirmed place stays where it is until staff confirm the handoff.</p>
  <p>Keep your existing schedule. After the practice, tell us which steps were clear, where anyone needed help and whether the roster ended as expected. Share process notes without volunteer names, contact details or private screenshots.</p>
  <div class="pilot-actions">
    <a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@charitology.org?subject=Charity%20OS%20shift%20handoff%20pilot&amp;body=I%20would%20like%20to%20discuss%20a%20practice%20shift.%0AMy%20role%3A%0A">Discuss a shift handoff pilot</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/blob/main/docs/VOLUNTEER_SHIFT_HANDOFFS.md#try-one-practice-shift">Read the practice steps</a>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="materials"><p class="eyebrow">Take the working documents</p><h2>Write down the scope and the learning.</h2><p>These editable Markdown briefs work in a text editor or on paper. They keep missing values, publication decisions, recurring-update permission and OS participation separate.</p><div class="pilot-downloads">{websitePilotMaterials.map(m=><a href={url(`/for-charities/website-pilots/materials/${m.id}.md`)} download={`${m.id}.md`}><strong>{m.title} ↓</strong><span>Editable Markdown · draft 0.1 · CC BY 4.0</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="prose"><h2>Automate preparation. Keep decisions explicit.</h2><p>A recurring workflow can check current public sources, prepare a revised private concept, retain a change list and queue a message for review. The website owner approves publication; recipients choose whether they want recurring updates, their purpose and cadence. A published inbox or past conversation supplies no automatic permission for a sequence.</p><p>Early concepts use public information and fictional records. Keep private donor, staff and beneficiary information out of a first message. Existing forms, payments, accounts, credentials and data integrations need their own agreed scope.</p></section>
<section class="prose"><h2>Join communities by contributing.</h2><p>Start with the group’s purpose, eligibility and current rules. Offer a useful answer or resource, ask organizers where a pilot invitation belongs and accept a refusal. Participation is not permission to harvest contacts or privately message members with a pitch.</p><p>Use the <a href={url('/for-charities/networks/')}>networks directory</a> to find peers and <a href={url('/for-charities/collaborate/')}>share a practical question</a>. These three starting points were checked against official sources on November 5, 2026. A listing does not establish membership, endorsement or permission to recruit.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="communities-title"><p class="eyebrow">Three places to begin · source review draft</p><h2 id="communities-title">Find the community that fits the contribution.</h2><div class="pilot-grid">{communities.map(c=><article><h3>{c.name}</h3><p>{c.body}</p><p>{c.limit}</p><ul>{c.links.map(([label,href])=><li><a href={href}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul></article>)}</div><p class="prose">Keep organizer replies and member information private. Ask about additional group rules; a community account does not authorize promotional messages.</p></section>
<ReviewNote filePath="src/pages/for-charities/website-pilots.astro" title="Website improvements and Charity OS pilots" />
</div>
</Base>
<style>
.pilot-body{padding-bottom:3rem}.pilot-body>section{margin-block:2rem 3rem}.pilot-actions{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.pilot-steps{list-style:none;padding:0;max-width:80ch}.pilot-steps>li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr;gap:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-block:1.4rem}.pilot-steps>li>span{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.8rem;color:var(--accent)}.pilot-steps h3{margin:0;font-size:1.6rem}.pilot-steps p{margin-bottom:0}.pilot-choice{padding:1.5rem;border-left:3px solid var(--accent);background:var(--surface);max-width:80ch}.pilot-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin-block:1.5rem}.pilot-grid article{border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1.3rem;min-width:0}.pilot-grid h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:0}.pilot-downloads{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:75ch}.pilot-downloads a{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.4rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1.2rem;color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none}.pilot-downloads span{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--ink-2)}a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}#pilot,#materials{scroll-margin-top:5rem}@media(max-width:680px){.pilot-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.pilot-steps>li{grid-template-columns:2rem 1fr;gap:.6rem}}
</style>
